de230dc","event_uuid":"782ec2ed-18eb-4680-96a5-f591c745debd","position":{"commit_sha":"0cd4865d9d641d2188f6e72dcd54c4eafddd5d5b","position":"1787868175606886486-782ec2ed-18eb-4680-96a5-f591c745debd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fa7bccbf8b8a7ddbee5fa92949797c4ec7d816341ef23aba232361f325493c83","event_uuid":"59969685-4804-438b-9c4e-3cf5449edfba","position":{"commit_sha":"b8ce67827b3825e59cabbe1ad75814a8dfbc79eb","position":"1787869867457452001-59969685-4804-438b-9c4e-3cf5449edfba"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9a0217113be920cdd53eb52c3f33a59f5b3502e7fbbc0cd2cb718cc96a508836","event_uuid":"d2d22559-c6be-4481-a8d1-c287e8fcd294","position":{"commit_sha":"d6f0c10bd19293175991a97af8096f16003dd456","position":"1787870214358006001-d2d22559-c6be-4481-a8d1-c287e8fcd294"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"81c73339150b3a484c52ea6d045bb65a87c32eacc90345165d3ad82256e0c467","event_uuid":"1cdf3c58-c5d0-4138-ae39-6cd53b250baf","position":{"commit_sha":"ba8eb9c23eb208e3eac00044ddfa5b234dafc970","position":"1787872160040630806-1cdf3c58-c5d0-4138-ae39-6cd53b250baf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as gerrit change 2277 (Change-Id I909a81fe). Guardrail rationale captured here rather than in the description to preserve the signed plan-review attestation: the probe's run_python tool executes arbitrary Python in-process. It is scoped to a workflow_dispatch-only diagnostic against a throwaway ephemeral Jira DC with no other secrets in the job; REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1 keeps rebar's own ticket store read-only; it is inert on every ordinary run (opt-in behind REBAR_DC_RICHTEXT_PROBE=1) and never runs on push/PR/schedule. This mirrors the existing scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py precedent. Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified before submit; ticket stays in_progress until landed.","timestamp":1787867633546119001}],"created_at":1787866613851413001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bdf62d06-660c-4570-8904-cdecf1af1f00","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"af1b-8e22-7ef4-477b"},{"link_uuid":"782ec2ed-18eb-4680-96a5-f591c745debd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c7c8-10c4-636a-4e5d"},{"link_uuid":"1cdf3c58-c5d0-4138-ae39-6cd53b250baf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"20b6-5b93-e5b8-40f2"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nThe working amd64 Jira Data Center harness only boots inside a CI runner (arm64 hosts stall\nunder emulation — `tests/external/live_jira_dc/README.md`). So every live DC reconcile\nobservation currently costs a full ~2h push→CI cycle, which makes root-causing live-only DC\ndefects (e.g. bug `reckless-diabolic-kob` — rich-text stored as `None` + perpetual re-emit)\nprohibitively slow.\n\n## Approach\n\nReuse the EXISTING agentic-in-CI pattern (`scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py` +\n`.github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml`, ticket 259b): boot the ephemeral DC ONCE, then\nrun an Opus agent on rebar's own `rebar.llm` runtime that performs MANY live experiments in\nthat single boot. Where capability-map's agent drives raw REST to *map* the image, this one\ndrives rebar's OWN reconcile primitives to *root-cause* a defect.\n\nNew files (test + CI only — no `src/rebar` change):\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_richtext_agentic_probe.py` — an opt-in pytest module\n  that reuses the proven `bound_dc_issue` fixture chain (so the agent starts from the exact\n  `(repo, local_id, key)` the failing rich-text tests use, cutover `dc` on) and boots the\n  agent with two tools: `run_python(code)` (a persistent in-process REPL warm-started with the\n  transport, `compute_update_fields`, `WikiTextCodec`, `cutover_clients`, `dc.run_bridge`,\n  `rebar`) and `jira_rest(method, path, body)` (raw REST ground-truth). Returns a structured\n  `RichTextRca` finding, each experiment cited to evidence ids.\n- `.github/workflows/jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml` — a `workflow_dispatch`-only driver, same\n  guardrails as capability-map (throwaway ephemeral instance, `REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1`, agent\n  instructed to REPORT not fix), installing `[dev]` (LLM runtime) + `[jira-datacenter]`\n  (transport), uploading the finding + evidence artifact.\n\n## Portability\n\nThe investigator is a **pytest module gated by env** (`REBAR_DC_RICHTEXT_PROBE=1` +\n`REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1` + an LLM credential + the harness skip markers), so it runs against ANY\nreachable live DC — a local `make jira-dc-up` instance or CI — not a single CI provider. The\nGitHub Actions workflow is one convenient trigger, not the only path; a contributor with a\nlocal DC + key runs the same test directly with `pytest`. It is inert on every ordinary run\n(opt-in off → skips), never on push/PR/schedule.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `test_dc_richtext_agentic_probe.py` exists, lint/format clean, and collects + skips\n      cleanly when the opt-in env is unset (no live DC required for collection).\n- [ ] The module reuses the existing `bound_dc_issue` / `dc_store_copy_repo` / `dc_transport`\n      fixtures rather than re-porting the bound-store bootstrap.\n- [ ] The agent is given `run_python` (persistent namespace) + `jira_rest` tools and returns a\n      registered structured `RichTextRca` contract; it asserts only that a finding was\n      produced (an investigation, not a correctness assertion — it must not fail merely\n      because the bug still reproduces).\n- [ ] `jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml` is `workflow_dispatch`-only (no push/PR/schedule), boots\n      the pinned DC image, installs both `[dev]` and `[jira-datacenter]`, requires an\n      `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (loud fail if absent), sets `REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1`, and uploads the\n      finding + evidence artifact.\n- [ ] A `workflow_dispatch` run of the probe on `main` completes and uploads a `RichTextRca`\n      finding with cited experiment evidence.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_richtext_agentic_probe.py","reason":"New opt-in agentic pytest module: reuses bound_dc_issue fixtures, boots rebar.llm agent with run_python+jira_rest tools, returns structured RichTextRca finding."},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml","reason":"New workflow_dispatch-only driver: boots the pinned ephemeral DC, installs [dev]+[jira-datacenter], runs the probe under guardrails, uploads finding+evidence."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py","reason":"Register the new workflow in the locked display-name table (_EXPECTED_NAMES) as required by test_every_workflow_is_named_in_the_locked_table."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","20b6-5b93-e5b8-40f2"],["relates_to","c7c8-10c4-636a-4e5d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"99a2cd84-fe92-4b47-862f-ed7273e2df48","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"bc5d-ffba-006b-4241","ticket_type":"task","title":"Reusable agentic in-CI Jira DC investigator (rich-text root-cause probe)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f9fa13e1-824f-4cf8-a001-6452aa4060e3","bdf62d06-660c-4570-8904-cdecf1af1f00","b9f28ade-a877-42b9-a1ec-4c41b266bd29","8acf995c-fd57-4b2b-be7f-e161ebaed0a4","8ad64af0-4111-4496-a47b-53c0636eca29","99a2cd84-fe92-4b47-862f-ed7273e2df48","7e2cc536-4f9a-4900-81a3-4451f9013f26","5ad1cbce-fbfe-458a-a44f-3c306377baec","b6c6a069-162b-49d9-8731-ff9645734637","782ec2ed-18eb-4680-96a5-f591c745debd","59969685-4804-438b-9c4e-3cf5449edfba","d2d22559-c6be-4481-a8d1-c287e8fcd294","1cdf3c58-c5d0-4138-ae39-6cd53b250baf"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787876731590740001,"uuid":"bc94cec1-f9ef-4a7a-b55a-68496eca8b1a"}